# The SuperDrastic release install.sh installs (https://github.com/JorreFog/SuperDrastic): version and the sha256 of
# superdrastic-<version>-aarch64.tar.gz. Bump both together. This release ships the package in dsflip/.
# 0.5.0-beta.1-rocknixds.7 is SuperDrastic v0.5.0-beta.1 (the in-game menu) plus
# dsflip/superdrastic-0.5.0-beta.1-rocknixds.7.patch (SuperDrastic branch claude/1-6-prep-work-kwq9lc and two commits
# made on an RG DS Plus, local branch 1.6-freeze-fix): 1.5.13's four
# commits (shader output sizes with ds-fsr at 3x on the RG DS Plus; the Wi-Fi / Nintendo WFC path; its pre-device
# fixes; the microphone's tunables, logs and joystick-button fallback) and 1.6's (the stall watch and a quit that works
# on a stuck game; new threads on every CPU; RetroAchievements logins that survive no network; online play only with
# DSFLIP_WFC; the menu's Blow on the fake microphone's real binding; DSFLIP_STALL_TEST; the in-game menu's pixel
# text on the font's grid at 640x480; DraStic's helper threads held until their locks exist, which was the freeze at
# a game's start). The same package on the RG DS and the RG DS Plus.
# Built with build.sh (clang 23 + lld, an Ubuntu noble arm64 sysroot: libc6 2.39, libdrm 2.4.125) and
# package.sh; it needs glibc 2.38 like the release. Once the patch is in a SuperDrastic release, pin that release here
# instead and drop the patch.
# 0.5.0-beta.1-rocknixds.9-test.1 (a PRIVATE test build, 2026-10-09; not a release): the RG DS line's .8 (the
# in-game menu's fixes and 3x's lines, SuperDrastic branch claude/open-issues-rocknix-nightly-1l4s4w) plus the 3x
# work, built from SuperDrastic's local branch opt/3x-a55-noil: the cache work of 2026-10-05 (prefetch in the pixel
# kernels, direct rendering into the scanout buffers, no copy of an unchanged 3D frame, audio without SDL's subsystem,
# test aids), SuperDrastic PR #8 (the rasterizer scheduled for the Cortex-A55; it also fixes 3x textures drawn askew)
# and #6 (3x keeps its own clock memory). Verified on this handheld: frames identical with and without PR #8 at 2x (six
# games), at 3x except where it now matches DraStic's own picture; 54 starts at 3x through this line's session.sh with
# the build before PR #8 without a freeze, and the final library in real sessions. Source: SuperDrastic's
# refs/testers/sd-9-test.1.
# 0.5.0-beta.1-rocknixds.9-test.4 (PRIVATE test build 4, 2026-10-11; not a release): test build 3's library merged
# into the Gengis Engine at SuperDrastic e646968 (2D scanline routines, geometry stage and A55-scheduled kernels
# replaced) with test build 3's cache work ported onto it (kernel and downsample prefetch, no copy of an unchanged
# 3D frame, direct rendering into the scanout buffers), 3x honouring disable_edge_marking, and issue 47's neighbour
# polygons at 3x. Measured on the RG DS Plus against test build 3: 3x faster in all four games tried (stress ROM
# 35.7 vs 34.9 fps at 1416 MHz, CPU a frame MKDS -4%, HeartGold -10%), 2x level; 2x exact (RAST=diff). Source:
# SuperDrastic's refs/testers/sd-9-test.4.
# 0.5.0-beta.1-rocknixds.9-test.6 (PRIVATE test build 6, 2026-10-11; not a release): test build 4's library with the
# CPU governor holding the power profile's bound from the start, and going past it (and remembering a clock as too
# slow) only when the game is CPU-bound. Test build 4 ran at 1992 MHz whatever the profile on the RG DS Plus. Source:
# SuperDrastic's refs/testers/sd-9-test.6.
